                <pb facs="0319" n="211" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg211"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Baker.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-08-15"><hi rendition="#italic">August 15,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 45.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 39 of the 6th ultimo, concerning the attempt of the Government of Nicaragua
                    to collect forced taxes. Adding that the Department approves your caution in
                    this class of property questions,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham</hi>,</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
